g  a part of things like this in 1968 I  worked with Gregory Peck on a picture  that's 50 years ago right now and I had  I asked him a couple of questions I said  how do you get into the Academy he was  the president of the Academy I think at  the time and he said you need more  credits and I said and how do you pick  material and he said you know when I was  a young actor I did not know the answer  to that and I asked a couple of actors  that I knew he said I asked Montgomery  Clift who said you do not take  everything they offer you you are very  careful about what you select you think  about it you feel it you live it through  you sleep on it you take your time and  you do not rush into something and  Gregory Peck said and you know I also  asked Gary Cooper how do you pick  material and Gary Cooper said you do  everything they hand you you never stop  working and you never pass up a day's  work and and Gregory Peck said and in  general they both had about the same  number of hits so it doesn't matter how  you do it only once in a great while  does something this could drop into your  lap I've said that before and it's true  and in Gregory Peck  then several years five years later was  my sponsor into the Academy so I was  yes I'm mighty grateful to be a member  of this organization thanks for being  here  thank you so much

